         <name>Fruit trees orchard</name>
         <description>Fruit trees include deciduous or evergreen trees, irrigated or rain-fed, as well as shrubs that produce either stone or pome fruits (apples, pears, apricots, cherries, peaches, plums, etc) along with exotic fruits such as avocados and mangoes. Satellite images are used to identify these orchards. Nurseries and planted pastures are not included in this category. The fruit trees is defined as such</description>
